============================================================
KEY LEARNINGS
============================================================

1. A subnet must be contained within the VNet address space.

2. NSGs can be associated with subnets.

3. NSGs contain both default security rules and custom security rules.

4. Default rules exist even when securityRules is empty.

5. Custom rules are returned under:
       securityRules

6. Default rules are returned under:
       defaultSecurityRules

7. NSG custom priorities range from:
       100-4096

8. Lower priority numbers are evaluated first.

9. Two rules cannot use the same priority in the same direction.

10. An NSG rule cannot simply be renamed through the update operation;
    deleting and recreating the rule is the practical approach.

11. JMESPath aliases are user-defined:

       --query "{Owner:tags.owner}"

    Here:
       Owner = user-defined output name
       tags.owner = Azure property being queried

12. Azure CLI command groups are hierarchical and must be correct.

13. Table output does not necessarily display every property.
    JSON is useful when inspecting complete resource details.

14. Resource IDs, subscription IDs, resource GUIDs, and ETags should
    not be copied into public lab documentation unnecessarily.

============================================================
END OF SESSION LOG
